      en: 'In automotive manufacturing every fitted part has to be traceable down to the last screw. Serial and batch numbers therefore go straight onto the metal or onto the label, and every station reads them into the system in real time. The hard part is not producing the code — it is keeping it readable years later, under oil, heat and washing.',
